   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of farmers from CBARD districts selling agricultural products to markets (domestic and international; direct and indirect beneficiaries)</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator tracks the total number of farmers from CBARD districts that sell their agricultural products to the targeted markets. It is understood that it is not possible to differentiate between CBARD direct beneficiaries and other farmers in the same districts for a number of reasons, and what is important is to ensure that aggregation of crops is sufficiently large as to make it worthwhile for traders to source from CBARD areas. Narrative descriptions of this target will need to also try and differentiate between the HVCs sold and other additional crops that may be grown in CBARD districts. For the purposes of CBARD, HVCs are defined as only those crops that have been strategically selected and analyzed by agricultural economists with clear justification for its selection as an HVC based on gross margin analysis, accompanied by a value chain study. Additional crops can be included, but will not be considered HVCs unless the aforementioned criteria is met.</narrative>
    </description>
